      "mergeID": "6639f6c3416f37fe57032a69",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I would like to have worlds with neither private nor public, so I want to allow members in my social groups to visit to my worlds with the restrict world attribute without my invitation. Thank you.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Restrict world for my group",
      "parentID": "5ca781ae2410314faa257f20",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "639a89e41fae6f7eb9461243",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ca77f240200d90e4ee65c5c|full_name}:  I wonder if by social group, they mean outside of VRChat.   I have a related issue in my classroom, having new users / students friend me is problematic. People just show up and expect things to work immediately. Heck the need to close VRChat and reopen (to get Web link to work) has been an issue for me. \n\nI wonder if we can reference an email account, one a person uses for VRChat, rather than a user name to grant access. Again, for me this is for new users who have not gotten accounts yet.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
